# goldens.tcyr -- rendered-audio regression goldens (2.0.3).
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. These checksums pin CHANGE DETECTION, not correctness. A
# green golden says "the audio is byte-for-byte what it was when the value was
# recorded"; it says nothing about whether that audio is right. Correctness
# lives in oracle_pins.tcyr (values derived from rust-old/) and hardening.tcyr.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. ghurni's semver rule is that a PATCH release may not change
# rendered audio -- but 2.0.1 and 2.0.2 both did, and nothing caught it either
# time. 2.0.1's was a miscompiled constant that made the gear/clock/engine decay
# envelopes 187x too flat, and the whole 135-assertion suite stayed green. This
# file is the gate that makes that impossible to repeat: if a checksum below
# moves, either the change was intended (bump a MINOR, write an ADR, and update
# the value in the same commit) or it is a bug.
#
# HOW TO UPDATE. Never "fix" a golden to make CI pass. Work out WHY it moved
# first. If the move is intended, record the reason in the CHANGELOG entry for
# the release that changes it.
#
# MOVED IN 2.8.0 (ADR-012, "Phase Continuity"). Seventeen moved, every one in a
# synth whose phase or ramps this release changed, and every one for a reason
# that is the point of the change, not a side effect of it:
#   engine (gasoline, diesel, two-stroke, all seven events): the crank angle is
#     integrated from the speed in force instead of position x current speed. Each
#     render starts with the smoother gliding from its 800 rpm default, so the old
#     crank was wrong from the first sample. MISFIRE also skips its whole firing
#     now, not one sample of it. Level change -1.07 to +0.77 dB (STALL, SHUTDOWN).
#   differential (both), chain: the same for the ring and chain phases, while
#     each smoother glides up from 0. Loaded and coasting also ramps its load and
#     coast terms. -0.45, -0.06 and +0.34 dB.
#   transmission (both): the loudness law reads a smoothed input rpm, so a fresh
#     gearbox fades in over its 50 ms smoother alongside its pitch, instead of
#     sounding at full level from sample 0 while the pitch rises from 0 Hz. The
#     shift case also ramps its load. -2.65 and -1.65 dB.
#   belt (both): the smoother it always advanced and discarded now drives its
#     loudness, flap and loop rate, so it fades in over 30 ms. -1.56 dB each.
# UNCHANGED, and that is ADR-012's central claim holding: a speed held from the
# first sample renders the old bits. Gear, motor, turbine, forced induction, the
# hybrid and all four clocks did not move, nor did the mixer goldens, which hold a
# gear and a motor. The clocks' tick windows became durations, which leaves the
# four default rates bit-identical.
#
# MOVED IN 2.3.0 (ADR-007). Six moved: the load SPECTRAL TILT touched every synth
# that takes a load (engine x3 including hybrid, motor, turbo), and differential
# gained ring-revolution modulation. Diesel moved twice over -- it also gained
# injection clatter. gear, transmission, turbine, clock, belt and chain take no
# load and were not touched, so they are bit-identical to 2.2.0.
#
# MOVED IN 2.2.0 (ADR-006). Five moved for the Depth changes: gear, transmission
# and differential gained mesh HARMONICS (they were pure sines); turbo's whine
# moved to blade-pass rate; chain gained its link-lap modulation. Two goldens
# were also FIXED rather than moved -- the clock window was widened from 0.5 s to
# 3 s because at 1 Hz it never contained a tock, and a hybrid golden was added
# because the engine type that changed most had none.
#
# MOVED IN 2.1.0 (ADR-005). Six of the eleven goldens changed when the RPM
# loudness law landed. They were updated deliberately, in the same commit as the
# change, with the reason recorded here:
#   engine (both)  the combustion pulse is now integrated across each sample
#                  instead of point-sampled, which removes the resonant-RPM
#                  amplitude notch; and the loudness law applies.
#   motor @4000    ref is 3000, so the gain at 4000 is 1.14, not 1.
#   turbine @8000  gain is exactly 1 at its 8000 reference -- this moved only
#                  because the noise SEED gained resolution (duct x1000).
#   differential   ref 3000, but its per-sample smoother converges to within an
#   chain @3000    ULP of target rather than exactly, so the gain is
#                  0.9999999..., which the 1e-6 quantizer can see.
# UNCHANGED, and that is the ADR's central claim holding: gear @1500,
# transmission @3000 and belt @2000 all sit exactly at their reference RPM, so
# their gain is exactly 1.0 and their audio is bit-identical. clock is exempt
# from the law entirely, and forced_induction already scaled via spool_rpm.
#
# QUANTIZATION. Samples are truncated to 1e-6 before hashing. ghurni's DSP leans
# on f64_sin / f64_cos / f64_exp / f64_pow, and a different platform's libm may
# differ in the last ulp; quantizing absorbs that while still catching any real
# audio change, which moves samples by orders of magnitude more. If a golden
# ever fails ONLY on a new platform, suspect libm before suspecting ghurni.

include "src/error.cyr"
include "src/logging.cyr"
include "src/dsp.cyr"
include "src/smooth.cyr"
include "src/event.cyr"
include "src/traits.cyr"
include "src/engine.cyr"
include "src/gear.cyr"
include "src/motor.cyr"
include "src/turbine.cyr"
include "src/clock.cyr"
include "src/transmission.cyr"
include "src/differential.cyr"
include "src/forced_induction.cyr"
include "src/belt_drive.cyr"
include "src/chain_drive.cyr"
include "src/mixer.cyr"
include "src/presets.cyr"

alloc_init();

var SR = f64_from(44100);

# FNV-ish offset basis, then a shift-xor-accumulate over the quantized samples.
# Order-sensitive: swapping two samples changes the result.
fn golden_ck(v) {
    var n = vec_len(v);
    var r = 1469598103;
    var i = 0;
    while (i < n) {
        var q = f64_to(f64_mul(vec_get(v, i), f64_from(1000000)));
        r = r + (q ^ (r << 1));
        i = i + 1;
    }
    return r;
}

# Every golden asserts the LENGTH too. A checksum alone would pass on an empty
# buffer, which is exactly the silent-failure shape 2.0.2 fixed in synthesize().
fn golden(v, want_len, want_ck, name) {
    assert_eq(vec_len(v), want_len, name);
    assert_eq(golden_ck(v), want_ck, name);
    return 0;
}

# ================================================================
test_group("golden: engine");
# ALL THREE MOVED IN 2.6.0 (ADR-010). The combustion pulse train now propagates
# down a quarter-wave waveguide and reaches the listener as the radiated field
# from the open end. Before 2.6.0 100% of it went straight out and the buffer
# labelled EXHAUST was an unrelated white-noise bed (ADR-009 s2). These are the
# only three golden assertions that move: all nine non-engine synths are
# bit-identical, which is the correct blast radius for a change confined to
# src/engine.cyr.
#
# gasoline: exhaust share 3.59% -> 64.3%, exhaust firing-period autocorrelation
# -0.040 -> +0.717, mono autocorrelation 0.654 -> 0.664 (the engine did NOT get
# less periodic to buy a periodic exhaust), level +0.21 dB.
golden(ghurni_engine_synthesize(ghurni_engine_new(GH_ENGINE_GASOLINE, 4, SR), f64_from(3000), 0.6, 0.1),
  4410, 0 - 5356771582266385321, "gasoline 4cyl @3000 load 0.6");
# diesel: same mechanism at the longer pipe its own resonance constant already
# implied -- f1 = 170 Hz is L = 0.81 m at c = 550 m/s, and a bigger engine really
# does carry a longer manifold. Level +0.57 dB.
golden(ghurni_engine_synthesize(ghurni_engine_new(GH_ENGINE_DIESEL, 6, SR), f64_from(1500), 0.9, 0.1),
  4410, 0 - 541103724187635529, "diesel 6cyl @1500 load 0.9");
# HYBRID had no golden before 2.2.0 -- the one engine type whose behaviour
# changed most had nothing pinning it.
#
# THIS ONE READS ALARMING AND IS NOT. duct_drive is 0 for HYBRID, so the EM whine
# and the (absent) combustion path are untouched. What changed is that the
# hybrid's small bed_gain=0.25 flow-noise term now traverses the duct instead of
# being the exhaust term directly. Measured level change: -0.004 dB. The checksum
# moves; the sound does not.
golden(ghurni_engine_synthesize(ghurni_engine_new(GH_ENGINE_HYBRID, 4, SR), f64_from(3000), 0.7, 0.1),
  4410, 8431386026841458236, "hybrid 4cyl @3000 load 0.7 (electric drive)");

